#{[17592186364182 #edb/ref 1080 "14" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364182 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364182 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "80193887-56ef-5f55-9899-81a4ca2a5bfa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364183 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364183 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364183 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d9ed3821-6db7-500c-afa6-af890beb1af8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364184 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364184 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364184 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee368a24-e35e-5530-bc4c-c0b11699a84f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364571 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364571 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95916" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364571 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364571 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The columns of $Q$ are orthonormal\n- $Q$ is a square matrix\n- $R$ is a square matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364571 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "14a18e20-8a94-54a8-afff-0a503b7d967c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364571 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis, they are orthonormal.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $Q$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix, it is square.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $R$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix, it is square.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364572 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364572 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364572 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364572 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364572 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364572 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364572 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364572 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186364573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364572 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "14c06a9a-d5bd-588b-bc25-ab1de6fdd166" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364573 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II, and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364573 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364573 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8dbe5dc9-2c40-591a-8dc9-2a6047634590" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364574 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364574 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364574 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "03859ee3-4c04-5da9-ac3f-9f5b14b65a8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364575 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364575 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364575 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8f52a007-3c47-5c22-8911-2baaae52e9c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364576 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364576 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364576 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "01eba2d3-fc91-5570-a105-b568905a237c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364577 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364577 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364577 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3901f3b0-6b91-5ac4-98c8-d16a45cdb47d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364585 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364585 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95931" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364585 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364585 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Q$ shown above. Find the matrix $R$ such that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364585 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "abcc772f-aef1-5bb8-8a2c-19affc4a7f6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364585 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $Q$ has orthonormal columns, pre-multiplying both sides of $A=QR$ by ${Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{T}\\cdot A & ={Q}^{T}\\cdot QR \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & =({Q}^{T}\\,Q)R \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & ={I}_{2}R \\\\ R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that ${Q}^{T}Q={I}_{2}$ since the columns of $Q$ are orthonormal.\n\nNow, we calculate the matrix $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364586 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref